<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:44:22 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>US war on Iran: Trump will ‘declare victory and go home’, embracing the ‘Greenland option’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260924-us-war-on-iran-trump-will-declare-victory-and-go-home-embracing-the-greenland-option</link><description>
François Picard welcomes Scott Anderson, journalist, war correspondent and best-selling author of "King of Kings: The Fall of the Shah and the Revolution That Forged Modern Iran". For Anderson, there is a striking parallel between 1979 and 2026: Washington’s persistent misreading of Iran, and the consequences that follow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/114dd1ee-b7b8-11f1-a2ef-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-183103-184712-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/114dd1ee-b7b8-11f1-a2ef-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-183103-184712-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">addc99fc-b7c0-11f1-b25b-89b269b94d7f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:35:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Turkey to hand over military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad</link><description>
Turkey will gradually hand over control of its Bashiqa military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad, Ankara and Baghdad said Wednesday, in a move aimed at strengthening Iraqi state authority and easing a long-running source of tension between the neighbours.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75398aa8-b7a5-11f1-98fb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26231257250409.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75398aa8-b7a5-11f1-98fb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26231257250409.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">49576f4e-b7ab-11f1-8e2c-3b35b9c82502</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:02:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75398aa8-b7a5-11f1-98fb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26231257250409.jpg">© Hadi Mizban, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb7ba0cc-b762-11f1-b0e3-c38db18beb93</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:49:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d3b7b0ca-b762-11f1-a655-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-23T143308Z-978379383-RC22PNAAB0P3-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg">© Mike Segar, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb495ca-b75e-11f1-ab5b-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-162850-163821-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3cb495ca-b75e-11f1-ab5b-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-162850-163821-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">422ed8b2-b75e-11f1-a0fb-b3e0727eeafd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:57:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1</link><description>
Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8cdb674-b75c-11f1-b426-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-161034-162844-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c8cdb674-b75c-11f1-b426-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-161034-162844-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ce3c89d2-b75c-11f1-bed7-fb2242db64af</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:44:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Golan Heights will 'remain Syrian', President Ahmed al-Sharaa vows at UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-golan-heights-will-remain-syrian-president-al-sharaa-vows-to-un</link><description>
Syria's President Ahmed al-Sharaa told the UN Wednesday that the contested Golan Heights region would "remain Syrian" despite ongoing military occupation by Israel. The Syrian leader also used his second turn at the UN rostrum to denounce repeated Israeli strikes on his country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16d963e0-b753-11f1-9328-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/29a71b1492a79ef56b3578045668a323a302b6b2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16d963e0-b753-11f1-9328-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/29a71b1492a79ef56b3578045668a323a302b6b2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">17619a1c-b753-11f1-b91f-9bb81ba5388b</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:31:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16d963e0-b753-11f1-9328-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/29a71b1492a79ef56b3578045668a323a302b6b2.jpg">© Timothy A Clary, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UN General Assembly enters second day with key speeches ahead</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/un-general-assembly-enters-second-day-with-key-speeches-ahead</link><description>
It’s Day Two of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, with a packed programme including speeches by Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky. Some of the biggest names in artificial intelligence will also address the UN Security Council. France 24’s Jessica Le Masurier is covering the gathering for us.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1c2ae1c-b74d-11f1-a548-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-140159-140614-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b804ab54-b74d-11f1-bac6-f70b2fc2239a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:10:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel denounces Macron's UN remarks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-denounces-macron-s-un-remarks</link><description>
Israeli officials have hit back at French President Emmanuel Macron after he criticised Israel’s conduct in the occupied West Bank during his address to the UN General Assembly. But while Macron used strong words against Israel, France allowed Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s plane to fly through French airspace on its way to New York, despite an ICC arrest warrant against him. Delano D’Souza reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f9be0b0-b744-11f1-92a6-833f01c30b8b/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-130719-130913-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8572b75c-b744-11f1-9d71-cd03806d7a8a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:56:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US President warns Tehran at UN but says talks ongoing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-warns-tehran-at-un-but-says-talks-ongoing</link><description>
The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani shares further insights.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f81f8c8-b73b-11f1-9bbb-55848da96185/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-120230-120511-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55615c0c-b73b-11f1-9c18-79ae88c1a4dc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:46:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel blasts ‘grotesque absurdity’ of Macron’s UN remarks on West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-israel-blasts-grotesque-absurdity-of-macron-s-un-remarks-on-west-bank</link><description>
The Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's office on Wednesday issued a stinging rebuke to French President Emmanuel Macron's UN speech denouncing settler violence against Palestinians in the West Bank. Macron's remarks that "Hamas has never struck in the West Bank" was a "grotesque absurdity", said the statement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18e616ae-b728-11f1-9937-cf792c3070f5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:41:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US President Trump threatens "annihilation" of Iran despite successful talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-president-trump-threatens-annihilation-of-iran-despite-successful-talks</link><description>
The day began with Donald Trump threatening to annihilate Iran but ended with a three-hour meeting between US and Iranian mediators, which Trump described as “very good.” Trump also held a high-level meeting with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, with both sides saying they wanted the war in Ukraine to end before winter. Today, as the UN General Assembly continues, Zelensky and Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian are among those expected to address the assembly, as world leaders seek ways to end the two conflicts dominating international politics. First, Morgan Ayre reports on the latest developments in the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5e96b4-b725-11f1-9742-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090239-090427-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef5e96b4-b725-11f1-9742-1d61c7110e09/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260923-090239-090427-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f5e239f0-b725-11f1-a102-f71ab3b91949</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:22:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>AI risks, Iran war dominate agenda at UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-ai-risks-iran-war-to-take-center-stage-at-un</link><description>
France convenes a UN Security Council meeting Wednesday on artificial intelligence (AI) and international security, which includes briefings by leading industry figures, including the heads of OpenAI and Anthropic. The meeting comes as world leaders jostle over how to address the risks of the new technology. On the second day of the UN General Assembly, the Iran war is also set to dominate the agenda. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2e4ad38-b70f-11f1-8b4a-75de2f89a542</guid><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:29:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d4dafa-86e8-11f1-a7c3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260723-C3244N4-v1-MidRes-DebateBetweenCandidatesForUnSecretaryGeneralPost.jpg">© Leonardo Munoz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran: Trump believes in an agreement after US midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260922-iran-trump-believes-in-an-agreement-after-us-midterms</link><description>
US President Donald Trump told the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday that he would have to decide whether to “annihilate” Iran if Tehran fails to reach a deal to end the war in the Middle East.
 
He added that he believed an agreement was possible after the US midterm elections in November.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8874df6-b6a1-11f1-939f-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-onu.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8874df6-b6a1-11f1-939f-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-onu.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e98a306-b6a1-11f1-9554-97e461cbcfd6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:17:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says envoys Witkoff, Kushner met with mediators on potential Iran deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260922-middle-east-live-yemen-fighting-escalates-as-trump-heads-to-un</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Tuesday said ‌special envoys ‌Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner had met ‌with mediators on a possible deal to end the US war against Iran. Trump earlier threatened to "annihilate the Islamic Republic" if Tehran didn’t reach a peace deal with Washington in his UN General Assembly speech. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">862bd6dc-b637-11f1-a4b2-b1db43887cfa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 03:41:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/418cfcc0-b698-11f1-84e6-d382746d948a/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265533113659.jpg">© Heather Khalifa, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia left without US help against Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-left-without-us-help-against-houthis</link><description>
Saudi Arabia is weighing Washington’s refusal to help fend off Houthi attacks after Riyadh requested US assistance, despite the two countries being longstanding allies and President Donald Trump and his family maintaining close personal ties with Saudi leaders. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details on this alliance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05396212-b5cc-11f1-ae0b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-160645-161307-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05396212-b5cc-11f1-ae0b-d5a6f2570fbe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-160645-161307-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a898152-b5cc-11f1-96e8-8756c005b286</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:57:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Two tankers hit by 'unknown projectile' or debris in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260921-projectile-hits-tanker-as-it-enters-the-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
Two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz on Monday by either an "unknown projectile" or debris, a maritime security agency said. United Kingdom Maritime Trade Operations added that at least two crew members were injured in the first incident, and both vessels will continue to their next port of call.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">515ed59e-b5bf-11f1-bfe2-bfc44b452264</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:03:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f53555d0-b5bf-11f1-acdf-e554abee39f5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26250323137076.jpg">©  Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: Israeli settler, Palestinian killed in latest violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-israeli-settler-palestinian-killed-in-latest-violence</link><description>
Violence flared in the Israeli-occupied West Bank on Sunday, as Israeli forces arrested a suspected Palestinian gunman accused of killing an Israeli man. In a separate incident, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian driver who the military said had attempted to run them over. Nicholas Rushworth reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeec1ca4-b5ba-11f1-abac-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-141854-142011-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eeec1ca4-b5ba-11f1-abac-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260921-141854-142011-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f40f9b02-b5ba-11f1-a271-7bd2a948b1ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:58:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings</link><description>
A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bfa79150-b504-11f1-829e-c100d0797634</guid><pubDate>Sun, 20 Sep 2026 15:30:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95da504c-b504-11f1-bc3f-5b4fdf021577/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26263426242066.jpg">© Mahmoud Illean, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>An Israeli settler and a Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings</link><description>
An Israeli settler has been fatally shot in the occupied West Bank, while Israel's military said it killed a man who attempted to ram his vehicle into troops elsewhere in the Palestinian territory. The news came as violence in the West Bank is escalating at a very rapid pace. “All Israeli military authorities involved with the West Bank have been warning the Israeli government that the situation is basically out of control”, explains FRANCE 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky.
